      "message": "fix(cli): every subcommand answers --help\n\nscript, process and mcp print their own usage (arguments and flags as\ntheir parsers read them) to stdout and exit 0 for --help or -h anywhere\nin their arguments. The check runs before the lane parses, so mcp --help\nnever starts the JSON-RPC server. Unknown flags still exit 2. The\ntop-level help points at `camcraft-cli <command> --help`.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/cli.rs: every_subcommand_answers_help_and_names_its_flags,\nhelp_flag_answers_anywhere_in_the_argv, mcp_help_does_not_start_the_server,\nunknown_flags_still_refuse_with_a_two_and_help_lists_per_command.\n\nFixes #1296\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
